added_lemmas.statement:
Let \(\vartheta\) have a continuously differentiable density that vanishes on the boundary of a bounded parameter domain and has finite prior Fisher-information matrix \(I_{\mathrm{pr}}\). In a dominated differentiable experiment with Fisher-information matrix \(I(\vartheta)\), every square-integrable estimator \(T\) of a differentiable scalar functional \(\psi(\vartheta)\) satisfies
\[
 \mathbb E\{T-\psi(\vartheta)\}^{2}
 \ge
 \{\mathbb E\nabla\psi(\vartheta)\}^{\!\top}
 \{I_{\mathrm{pr}}+\mathbb E I(\vartheta)\}^{-1}
 \{\mathbb E\nabla\psi(\vartheta)\},
\]
with the scalar formula as the one-dimensional special case.
